<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "In SKG-IF, it is used in the following classes (domain):\n* skos:Concept\n\nIn SKG-IF, it is used to link to entities belonging to the following classes (range):\n* skos:ConceptScheme" .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The classification scheme or vocabulary that a Topic term belongs to." .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "skos:inScheme (SKG-IF labels: defined_in)" .
